  "published": "2026-10-30T05:44:31.127Z",
  "releaseNotes": "## Version 10.6.0 - October 30, 2026\n\n  - **Improved:** Document Viewer:\n\n    - **Fixed:** Linux/MacOS support for Spreadsheet, Presentation, Diagram, ProjectManagement, Cad and Imaging formats.\n      We downgraded `System.Drawing.Common` package dependency from `6.0.0` to `5.0.3` as it turns out,\n      `PlatformNotSupportedException` was thrown in net6.0+ projects (e.g. net8.0 or net10.0) not from the runtime but\n      from the DLLs in the `6.0.0` package itself. So as long as we stay at `5.0.3`, we can still use `libgdiplus` on Linux/MacOS.\n      If you also have a separate dependency in your project to this package, make sure it's kept at `5.0.3` as maximum.\n      Now every format conversion or viewing works the same as Windows on Linux/MacOS.\n    \n    - **Improved:** Stability and performance of Pdf, WordProcessing, Spreadsheet, Presentation, Diagram, ProjectManagement, \n      Email formats.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "File manager control for integrating file browsing, upload & download features into your ASP.NET application or site (WebForms or MVC) rapidly.",
  "title": "ASP.NET File Manager and ASP.NET File Uploader",
